here are the best and worst outcomes of  the midterm elections the best Jerry the  best even the Republican stalwarts at  Fox News agree that the GOP take over  the Senate was a protest vote against  President Obama has failed Democratic  policies not an endorsement of Mitch  McConnell in the Republican agenda it's  always good to see politicians held  accountable the best Jerry the best  voters in Alaska Oregon in Washington DC  legalized recreational marijuana dealing  yet another body blow to the war on  drugs a majority in Florida backed  medical marijuana but the initiative  fell short of the 60 percent necessary  for legalization the best Jerry the best  Democrat Gina Raimondo became governor  of Rhode Island despite being opposed by  public sector unions for her central  rolling raining in out-of-control  pension plans Republican Governor Scott  Walker in Wisconsin and rick Snyder and  Michigan were reelected despite their  taking on public sector unions as well  the worst Jam voters in four states  approved hikes in the minimum wage  whatever the intentions might be making  workers more expensive by legislative  Fiat will only make it that much harder  for the most unskilled people to find  jobs the worst Jerry the People's  Republic of Berkeley overwhelmingly  passed the country's first real sin tax  on soda the tax will increase the cost  of a 20-ounce soda by ten percent the  worst Jam the bipartisan Budget  agreement reached earlier this year  increased spending levels beyond  sequestration and while many of the new  Republican senators were vague about  what programs they would cut while  campaigning they all pledged to support  extra defense spending and to protect  and preserve Social Security and  Medicare that almost certainly means  spending hikes over the next two years  for reason TV I'm Nick Gillespie
 

